-- title:
--   Positive elements of the closed ideal of a properly infinite element are Cuntz-below it
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a unital C*-algebra with its usual order. For $u,v\in A$ write $u\precsim v$ if $u\in\overline{\{\,w^*\,v\,w:\ w\in A\,\}}$. For self-adjoint $v\in A$ let
--   $$J(v)=\overline{\operatorname{span}\{\,x\,v\,y:\ x,y\in A\,\}}$$
--   be the closed two-sided ideal generated by $v$. An element $v\in A$ is *properly infinite* if there are row matrices $r_j=(r_j^{(1)},r_j^{(2)})$ with entries in $A$, $j\in\mathbb{N}$, such that $r_j^*\,v\,r_j=\bigl((r_j^{(k)})^*\,v\,r_j^{(l)}\bigr)_{k,l=1,2}$ converges to $\operatorname{diag}(v,v)$ in $M_2(A)$.
--
--   Let $u,v\in A$ with $u\ge0$, $v\ge0$, $v$ properly infinite and $u\in J(v)$. Then
--   $$u\precsim v.$$
--
--   For a properly infinite positive element, Cuntz domination by $v$ is therefore as large as it can be: it covers every positive element of the closed ideal generated by $v$. This converts ideal membership, which can be detected through representations, into a Cuntz comparison.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $J(v)$ is `closedIdeal v hv.isSelfAdjoint`, proper infiniteness is `ProperlyInfinite v` from the comparison module (`FiniteCuntzLE (doubleCorner v) (scalarCorner v)`), and the relation is `ScalarCuntzLE u v`. The order is `CStarAlgebra.spectralOrder`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/CStarAlgebra/PureInfiniteness/IdealComparison.lean#L94-L107

